Kubeadm Installation Guide

* Login into AWS account – launch 3 instances – AlmaLinux 9.

Master must have 2 vCPU and 4 GB RAM.

* Now, create or select a key pair and save the private key.
* Access all 3 instances (1 Master, 2 Nodes) using SSH or PuTTY.
Expose port 6443 in the Security Group to allow worker nodes to join the cluster.
Expose port 22 in the Security Group to allows SSH access to manage the instance..

* Commands common for Master & Node:--
```bash
sudo dnf update -y
sudo dnf install -y curl wget vim tar iproute-tc
 
* Now install the required packages for Kubernetes.
sudo swapoff -a
* Disable swap on all 3 instances:
```bash
cat <<EOF | sudo tee /etc/modules-load.d/k8s.conf
overlay
br_netfilter
EOF

* Load the required kernel modules:
```bash
sudo modprobe overlay
sudo modprobe br_netfilter
 
* Configure networking on all 3 instances:
cat <<EOF | sudo tee /etc/sysctl.d/k8s.conf
net.bridge.bridge-nf-call-iptables  = 1
net.bridge.bridge-nf-call-ip6tables = 1
net.ipv4.ip_forward                 = 1
EOF

sudo sysctl --system
lsmod | grep br_netfilter
lsmod | grep overlay


* Now install containerd on all 3 instances.
```bash
sudo dnf update -y 
sudo dnf install -y dnf-plugins-core ca-certificates curl
sudo install -m 0755 -d /etc/pki/rpm-gpg
sudo dnf config-manager --add-repo https://download.docker.com/linux/centos/docker-ce.repo
sudo dnf install -y containerd.io

 
sudo mkdir -p /etc/containerd
containerd config default | sudo tee /etc/containerd/config.toml > /dev/null

 
sudo sed -i \
  -e 's/SystemdCgroup = false/SystemdCgroup = true/' \
  -e 's|sandbox_image = "registry.k8s.io/pause:3.8"|sandbox_image = "registry.k8s.io/pause:3.9"|' \
  -e 's|sandbox_image = "registry.k8s.io/pause:3.6"|sandbox_image = "registry.k8s.io/pause:3.9"|' \
  /etc/containerd/config.toml

 
sudo systemctl enable containerd
sudo systemctl restart containerd
sudo systemctl status containerd --no-pager

grep -n 'SystemdCgroup\|sandbox_image' /etc/containerd/config.toml

 

*Install Kubernetes Components:
 ```bash
sudo dnf install -y curl ca-certificates

sudo tee /etc/yum.repos.d/kubernetes.repo > /dev/null <<'EOF'
